  "original_question": "Compare Karnataka and Tamil Nadu Engineering institutions in 2025.",
  "answer": "## Comparative Analysis: Engineering Institutions in Tamil Nadu and Karnataka (2025)\n\nBased on the 2025 NIRF Engineering rankings, Tamil Nadu exhibits a higher volume of ranked institutions and stronger performance metrics compared to Karnataka within the top 100 cohort.\n\n### Key Findings\n* **Institutional Volume:** Tamil Nadu has 14 distinct institutions in the top 100, while Karnataka has 7.\n* **Elite Ranking Presence:** Tamil Nadu shows a higher concentration of top-tier institutions, with 2 institutions in the top 10 and 10 in the top 50. In contrast, Karnataka has 0 institutions in the top 10 and 1 in the top 50.\n* **Performance Metrics:** Tamil Nadu recorded an average score of 59.85 and a median score of 58.53, compared to Karnataka's average score of 51.79 and median score of 49.26.\n* **Parameter Performance:** Tamil Nadu also leads in key parameters, with an average Research and Professional Practice (RPC) score of 50.3 (compared to 35.94 for Karnataka) and an average Teacher-Learner Ratio (TLR) of 74.71 (compared to 70.21 for Karnataka).\n\n### Summary Table\n| Metric | Tamil Nadu (2025) | Karnataka (2025) |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: |\n| Distinct Institutions (Top 100) | 14 | 7 |\n| Top 10 Institutions | 2 | 0 |\n| Top 50 Institutions | 10 | 1 |\n| Average Score | 59.85 | 51.79 |\n| Average RPC | 50.3 | 35.94 |\n| Average TLR | 74.71 | 70.21 |",
